WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.560
Punjab, 1849.

2
00:00:02.610 --> 00:00:05.110
The British annex the Sikh kingdom.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:10.060
At many Sikh weddings, a Brahmin priest
leads the couple around a sacred fire.

4
00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:14.230
Images of Hindu deities stand in the
precincts of the Harmandir Sahib.

5
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:18.470
Today, a Sikh couple walks around
the Guru Granth Sahib instead.

6
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:21.930
So who decided what
counts as Sikh practice?

7
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.770
And did they rediscover it, or invent it?

8
00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:28.530
In this mission, you'll lay out
the old codes of Sikh conduct,

9
00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:30.130
each slightly different.

10
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.850
Then you'll weigh up whether that code is
an effective guide to Sikh living today.

11
00:00:34.900 --> 00:00:39.230
Your mission: find out who decided
what counts as Sikh practice,

12
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.950
and whether they rediscovered
it or invented it.
